{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/residentclient carries the liveness probe, at head c50f0b0bb11014efa83420aede26f048cc2db675 on request/multi-resident-coordination, on main 2abe1cac. This replaces the retired candidate 834553e688478c739bf7e233ba311fde61cbc007 at head 1ccad3e2. Nothing in this package changed: both files are byte-identical to the reviewed candidate, and the whole delta from 1ccad3e2 is the one-byte final newline in internal/gitstore/gitstore.go.\n\nProbeResident asks a claimed address whether it is still serving that workroom, over the existing bounded, no-redirect, credential-free transport. Only a refused dial is a definitive negative and frees a claim; a timeout, a port that accepts and never answers, an unparseable or oversized answer, an answer naming another workroom, and a URL this client will not dial all return Ambiguous and leave the claim standing. The asymmetry is deliberate: a false negative starts a second resident beside a live one, a false positive only refuses to start.\n\nThe probe is where the untrusted input is handled. A claim is an ordinary repository file, so its URL goes through the same ValidateURL loopback check as every other resident call before anything is dialled; without it, starting a service would be a request forgery against whatever address a local writer chose. The answer is bounded by IdentityLimit at 4 KiB and decoded with unknown fields disallowed. The probe lives here rather than in internal/app because this package already knows how to speak to a resident and which addresses are safe, and because internal/residentclient depends on internal/app rather than the reverse; internal/app takes a Prober from its caller instead.\n\nTests at this head, in internal/residentclient/client_test.go: a resident answering for this workroom probes Alive and is asked only GET /v0/identity; a port answering for a different workroom probes Ambiguous; an unparseable answer probes Ambiguous; a listener that accepts and never answers probes Ambiguous under a short deadline; a closed port probes Dead, which is what stale-owner recovery depends on; and six claim URLs — a public address, a name, https, embedded credentials, a path, and empty — are each Ambiguous and never dialled.\n\nGates at this exact head: gofmt -l empty; go vet ./... clean; go test -count=1 ./... exit 0, 25 packages ok.\n\nThe live predecessor at this path is codex's 69e94d197f165a0c438a0eb7a3522edef8969b1c, for my merge to retire later; it is codex's record, so codex or hugh must retire it.\n\nGoverned by request 78963842b2a9e67962d350db9a4d7bf72a07fe85 and direction proposal v3 998918b6a065170ab1558f6a1d1d37dc12477aa6, approved in report eb555d7eed99c8275b91cdf2224d6c0e1942cc01, ratified 726335d9.","body":{"commit":"c50f0b0bb11014efa83420aede26f048cc2db675","path":"internal/residentclient"}}